  "description": "All 706 stations served by Europe's night trains — every station referenced by at least one service in the Open Night Train Database, snapshot **2026-08**, curated by [Back-on-Track Europe](https://back-on-track.eu/).\n\nEach point carries the station name (which is also the join key used across the ONTD), its country, and `n_services` — the number of night-train services calling there (derived; see the [agent guide](AGENTS.md)). The biggest hubs by this measure are Lviv (85), Kyiv (82) and — first outside Ukraine — München Ost (31).\n\nCoordinates were drafted from [OpenStreetMap](https://www.openstreetmap.org/)/Nominatim and human-verified by ONTD volunteers; `coord_backfilled` marks positions recovered by the mirror's retroactive backfill (the \"Coordinate provenance\" style shows this). Coordinates are therefore published under ODbL with OSM attribution.",
